#!/usr/bin/env beg

Accept one argument, the path to the JSON file to update.
Fetch the National parks table from https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_national_parks_of_the_United_States.

Write a JSON array sorted by park name. Each entry has a name, a locations array
of state or territory names, an established date in YYYY-MM-DD format, and acres
as a number. Use the values in the table and omit citations and coordinates.

Validate the complete table and any existing JSON before atomically replacing
the file. Leave an identical file untouched. Print one line per added, removed,
or changed park in the form `added Acadia`, or print `up to date` when they match.
On failure, explain the problem on stderr and leave the existing file intact.
